[[:db/retract 17592186351078 :question/answer-fields 17592186351079] {:db/id "q-161286/absolute-v-v1/selection/correct-answer" :answer/id #uuid "014fc7ab-4b27-5855-99e0-5a6eca199801" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u)\\sqrt{8}|v|" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-161286/absolute-v-v1/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2a33f854-4bfe-5310-8686-d5eed1146d88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices [17592186351080 17592186351081 17592186351082 17592186351083 17592186351084 "q-161286/absolute-v-v1/selection/correct-answer"] :answer-field/correct "q-161286/absolute-v-v1/selection/correct-answer" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186351078 :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=-x-y-z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2}-{u}^{2},\\,u⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ Use the scalar surface-area factor $\\|r_u\\times r_v\\|$ with its absolute values for the stated parameter domain. What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a scalar surface integral, the pullback integrand is $f(r(u,v))\\|r_u\\times r_v\\|$. The derivatives and cross product are\n\n$$r_u=(1,-2u,1),\\qquad r_v=(0,2v,0),\\qquad r_u\\times r_v=(-2v,0,2v).$$\n\nThus the nonnegative area factor is\n\n$$\\|r_u\\times r_v\\|=\\sqrt{(-2v)^2+(2v)^2}=\\sqrt8\\,|v|.$$\n\nSubstitution into the scalar function gives\n\n$$f(r(u,v))=-u-(v^2-u^2)-u=u^2-v^2-2u.$$\n\nThe missing integrand for the stated general parameter domain is therefore\n\n$$(u^2-v^2-2u)\\sqrt8\\,|v|.$$\n\nThe source omitted the absolute value and supplied no sign restriction on $v$. Its option $(u^2-v^2-2u)\\sqrt8\\,v$ is valid on a positive-$v$ patch, but fails when $v<0$: at $(u,v)=(1,-1)$ the corrected value is $-2\\sqrt8$, while that source option gives $2\\sqrt8$. The capture used a distinct explicit $v>0$, regular, one-to-one recovery request. This study question retains the original domain and supplies the correct absolute-value choice.\n\nThe parametrization loses rank at $v=0$. As usual, interpreting the displayed equality as an integral over the surface assumes regular patches and no multiple coverage except on negligible boundaries; the local area factor remains $\\sqrt8|v|$." :question/answer-fields ["q-161286/absolute-v-v1/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
